{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every default placeholder ships two independent levers: a "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"style"}]},{"type":"text","text":" (how big a footprint it expects to own) and, in SwiftUI, a "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"theme"}]},{"type":"text","text":" (what color\/font it uses). On top of the default spinner, two alternative Loading placeholders cover the other common shapes a loading state takes: a pulsing skeleton, and a redacted mirror of the real content."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"compact-style","text":"`.compact` style","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStatePlaceholderStyle","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" controls how much space a default placeholder expects to fill. Every default placeholder’s initializer takes a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"style:"},{"type":"text","text":" parameter, defaulting to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".standard"},{"type":"text","text":" — the full-screen treatment: a full-size icon, and, for the Loading spinner, filling all available space."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Pass "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".compact"},{"type":"text","text":" to embed the same placeholder in a card or section instead of a whole screen: a smaller icon, smaller text, and — for the Loading spinner — no more forcing itself to fill the available space:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["ScreenStateDefaultEmptyView(style: .compact)","ScreenStateDefaultLoadingUIView(style: .compact)"],"syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":".compact"},{"type":"text","text":" always keeps a vertical icon-above-text layout, regardless of the device’s orientation — a card’s size is dictated by the card, not the device, unlike the automatic landscape-iPhone icon-beside-text switch "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".standard"},{"type":"text","text":" makes on its own."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Alternative-Loading-placeholders","text":"Alternative Loading placeholders","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDefaultLoadingView","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDefaultLoadingUIView","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" — the spinner — are what every default-wired "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScreenStateView"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScreenStateContainerView"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScreenStateViewController"},{"type":"text","text":" shows. Two opt-in alternatives cover the other common shapes a loading state takes:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateShimmerLoadingView","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateShimmerLoadingUIView","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":": a pulsing skeleton of a circular avatar plus two text-line placeholders, for a generic “something’s coming” look that doesn’t need to know the real content’s shape."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateRedactedLoadingView","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":": renders your real content view through SwiftUI’s "},{"code":".redacted(reason: .placeholder)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so the placeholder mirrors the exact shape of the content it’s standing in for. SwiftUI-only — "},{"code":"redacted(reason:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" has no UIKit equivalent."}]}]}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["ScreenStateShimmerLoadingView()","","ScreenStateRedactedLoadingView {","    ArticleRow(article: .placeholder)","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Both respect Reduce Motion and Increase Contrast the same way the default spinner does; see "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/Accessibility","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Theming","text":"Theming","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStatesTheme","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" lets a SwiftUI app theme every default placeholder at once — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tint"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"titleFont"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"messageFont"},{"type":"text","text":" — instead of passing a fully custom placeholder view at every call site. Set it once via "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"View.screenStatesTheme(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" on a container view, and every default placeholder beneath it in the view hierarchy (including "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateShimmerLoadingView","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":") picks it up:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["MyScreenView()","    .screenStatesTheme(ScreenStatesTheme(tint: .indigo, titleFont: .title2, messageFont: .callout))"],"syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Any property left "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" (the default, via "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStatesTheme\/standard","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":") keeps the built-in gradient\/font. Increase Contrast still wins over "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tint"},{"type":"text","text":" regardless — it’s an accessibility need, not a branding preference."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"There’s no UIKit equivalent: UIKit has no concept of an inherited environment, so the UIKit default placeholders keep taking their configuration directly through their initializers."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/screenstates\/styling"]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/Styling"},"kind":"article","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates"]]},"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The built-in style variants, alternative Loading placeholders, and the theming configuration point — everything beyond the out-of-the-box defaults for tuning how a placeholder looks without writing a fully custom one."}],"metadata":{"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article","title":"Styling","modules":[{"name":"ScreenStates"}]},"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDefaultEmptyView","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDefaultLoadingView","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDefaultErrorView","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/Accessibility"],"anchor":"Related-Documentation","title":"Related Documentation"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenSt